3. The Commission shall update the list of countries where necessary, including where new agreements are concluded or circumstances change.
4. The implementing acts shall also provide for periodic monitoring of these criteria. The initial list shall be adopted within six months by the entry into force of this Regulation.
5. The Commission shall monitor trade flows and market developments, in particular to detect:
a) unusual increases in imports indicating possible circumvention;
b) distortions identified in trade defence or anti-subsidy cases;
c) inconsistencies between trade flows and production capacity.
Where necessary, the Commission may adopt measures, including suspending or limiting the recognition of originating content, or excluding a third country, in accordance with the applicable procedures.
6. By way of derogation from the provisions of paragraph 1, Union origin requirements applicable to vehicles and his components with addition of corporate low emission vehicles in the context of public procurement procedures referred to in Annex III, the definition of “equivalent content of origin” shall be include only products and components originating from the UK.

2.The Commission shall adopt implementing acts pursuant to Article 5 of Regulation (EU) No 182/2011 to establish and update the lists of third countries whose originating products and components may be considered equivalent to Union-origin content.
In preparing those implementing acts, the Commission shall assess, in particular:
(a) whether the third country grants effective and reciprocal access to Union products and economic operators under the relevant agreements;
(b) whether its inclusion could create or increase strategic dependencies or otherwise threaten the security of supply in the Union;
(c) the existence of reservations, sectoral limitations, thresholds, localisation or local content requirements, national preferences or other restrictions;
(d) whether fair competition conditions are ensured, including the absence of discriminatory measures, distortive subsidies or other practices that could undermine the level playing field;
(e) the risk of circumvention of the requirements laid down in Article 12.The Commission shall also take into account any applicable exceptions and the dispute-settlement provisions of the relevant agreements.
3. The Commission shall regularly review the country lists and amend them, where necessary, by means of implementing acts pursuant to Article 5 of Regulation (EU) No 182/2011, including where a third country concludes a new agreement or where the conditions referred to in paragraph 2 are no longer met.
4. The implementing acts shall establish a procedure for the periodic monitoring of the criteria set out in paragraph 2. The first implementing act establishing the lists shall be adopted within six months of the entry into force of this Regulation.
5. The Commission shall monitor trade flows and market developments at least annually in order to identify significant increases in imports, evidence of circumvention, trade-defence or anti-subsidy concerns, or discrepancies between trade flows and production capacity indicating possible transhipment.Where such risks are identified, the Commission may suspend or limit the equivalence of a third country and may, by means of delegated acts pursuant to Article 30, exclude that third country, in whole or in part, from the scope of paragraph 1.
6. By way of derogation from paragraph 1, for the Union-origin requirements applicable to vehicles and their components, including corporate low-emission vehicles under the public support schemes referred to in Annex III, “equivalent content of origin” shall include only products and components originating in the United Kingdom.

2b.In addition to the requirements laid down in paragraph 2 of this Article, contracting authorities and contracting entities shall include a factor in the award criteria for the relevant procedures that rewards tenders containing a high proportion of manufacturing operations physically carried out in the Union, within the meaning of Article 3(1), point 41a. That award criterion:
