Part IIIa – Bonus for zero-emission heavy-duty vehicles
For the purpose of considering vehicles as 'made in the EU' in the context of the incentive mechanisms provided for in Regulation (EU) 2019/1242, the following criteria apply:
1. the cab of the vehicle is manufactured in the Union;
2. the vehicle is assembled in the Union;
3. and one of the three criteria below:
(a) the ratio between the total ex-works price of vehicle components – excluding the vehicle battery – originating in the Union and the total ex-works price of all vehicle components – excluding the battery – is equal to or greater than 75%; or
